259 - Draw Us in the Spirit's Tether
 / 
Key: G
Time: 4/4
Tempo: Moderato
Number: 259
Topic: Holy Spirit - 

Verse 1:
[Bm]Draw [D]us [Em]in [Am]the [G]Spirit's [D7]tether,
[G]For [C]when [Bm]humbly [G]in [Am]Thy [Bm]name,
[G]Two or three [F#dim]are [D]met [G]together,
[C]Thou [Bm]art [Am]in [G]the [Am]midst [Bm]of [Am]them;
[G]Alleluia! [D]Alleluia!
[G]Touch we [Bm]now [Am]Thy [G]garment's hem.

Verse 2:
[Bm]As [D]the [Em]brethren [G]used [Em]to [D7]gather
[G]In [C]the [Bm]name [Am]of [G]Christ [Am]to [Bm]sup,
[G]Then with thanks [F#dim]to [D]God [G]the [D]Father
[C]Break [Bm]the [Am]bread [G]and [Am]bless [Bm]the [Am]cup,
[G]Alleluia! [D]Alleluia!
[G]So knit [Bm]Thou [Am]our [G]friendship up

Verse 3:
[Bm]All [D]our [Em]meals [Am]and [G]all [Em]our [D7]living
[G]Make [C]us [Bm]sacraments [Am]of [Bm]Thee,
[G]That by caring, [D]helping, giving,
[C]We [Bm]may [Am]true [G]disciples [Am]be.
[G]Alleluia! [D]Alleluia!
[G]We will [Bm]serve [Am]Thee [G]faithfully.
